# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/incidents.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event inc_fever_bill
# en: A Fever and a Bill
title [a86a8d] = 一场高烧，一张账单
# en: You wake in the infirmary with a fever that makes the ceiling breathe. Sister Amaranth holds up a small blue bottle. "This clears it by morning. It is also not free," she says. "Or you can sweat it out, like your ancestors."
text [9f097a] = 你在医务室醒来，烧得连天花板都像在呼吸。阿玛兰斯修女举起一只蓝色小瓶。“这个能让你明早退烧。它也不是免费的，”她说，“要不然你就像你的祖先那样，硬扛过去。”
# en: A pale student in an infirmary bed, a stern nurse holding out a small blue bottle and a folded bill.
scene [b357c5] = 医务室病床上一个脸色苍白的学生，一位严厉的修女递来一只蓝色小瓶和一张折好的账单。
# en: Buy the tonic
opt.left.label [424c55] = 买下药剂
# en: {~It tastes of tin and regret.|It tastes like a pond that has given up.} By morning the ceiling is a ceiling again, and your purse is noticeably lighter.
opt.left.say.1 [b9ca12] = {~它尝起来像锡和悔恨。|它尝起来像一潭放弃了的池水。}到了早上，天花板又只是天花板了，你的钱袋却明显轻了一截。
# en: Sweat it out
opt.right.label [cf0e70] = 硬扛过去
# en: Three days of damp sheets and strange dreams about stairs. You miss a week of notes, and come back feeling like a wrung-out dishcloth.
opt.right.say.1 [fe076d] = 三天的湿床单，还有一堆关于楼梯的怪梦。你漏了一整周的笔记，回来时整个人像一块拧干的抹布。

@event inc_broken_wand
# en: Snapped on the Stairs
title [fbb3ae] = 断在楼梯上
# en: The moving stairs shift without warning. You catch yourself; your wand doesn't. It lies in two pieces on the landing, still fizzing at the break like a sulking firework.
text [e32b26] = 移动楼梯毫无预兆地挪了位置。你稳住了自己，你的魔杖却没有。它断成两截躺在平台上，断口还在嘶嘶冒火花，像一支赌气的烟花。
# en: A student kneeling on a stone staircase, holding the two halves of a wand that still fizzes faintly at the break.
scene [8c70b7] = 一个学生跪在石阶上，手里捧着断成两截的魔杖，断口仍微微冒着火花。
# en: Have it properly rebound
opt.left.label [97789e] = 找人好好修
# en: The repairer in the village tuts, splints it with silver wire and charges you for every tut. It works better than before, which is somehow worse.
opt.left.say.1 [d64a94] = 山下小镇的修理匠啧啧连声，用银丝把它绑好，每啧一声都算了钱。它比以前更好用了，这反倒更让人憋屈。
# en: Bind it with string and hope
opt.right.label [1dbf63] = 拿绳子绑上，听天由命
# en: It holds. It spits a little when you cast, like a cat that forgives you but wants it noted.
opt.right.say.1 [75ab3f] = 它撑住了。施法时会稍微啐一下，像一只原谅了你、但要你记住这笔账的猫。
# en: It holds for three days, then sneezes a spell backwards. Your eyebrows grow back within the week; your marks take longer.
opt.right.say.2 [76926c] = 它撑了三天，然后打了个喷嚏，把一道咒语倒着放了出去。你的眉毛一周内就长回来了，你的成绩可没那么快。

@event inc_library_fine
# en: The Overdue Notice
title [716b08] = 逾期通知
# en: A prefect in a red sash slides a notice across your desk. The library book you borrowed has come back late, damp and, somehow, with teeth marks. "Damages," she says. "Or you can argue. People do. It never goes well."
text [14a576] = 一位系着红绶带的级长把一张通知推到你桌上。你借的那本图书馆的书逾期归还，湿漉漉的，还不知怎么多了一圈牙印。“赔偿，”她说，“或者你也可以争辩。有人这么干过。从来没好结果。”
# en: A prefect in a red sash holding out a long paper notice, a book with teeth marks on the desk between them.
scene [618e44] = 一位系红绶带的级长举着一张长长的纸质通知，两人之间的桌上放着一本带牙印的书。
# en: Pay the fine
opt.left.label [4e47fa] = 交罚款
# en: She stamps your receipt with great satisfaction. The book is reshelved in a cage, which feels like the right outcome for everyone.
opt.left.say.1 [197c1b] = 她心满意足地在你的收据上盖了章。那本书被重新上架——关进了笼子里，这对大家来说似乎都是最好的结局。
# en: Argue that the book bit first
opt.right.label [ab548f] = 坚称是书先咬的
# en: You produce the bite on your thumb as evidence. The prefect inspects it, then the book, and halves the fine to nothing. "Fair," she says. "It has a history."
opt.right.say.1 [672cfa] = 你亮出拇指上的咬痕作为证据。级长检查了它，又检查了那本书，把罚款一笔勾销。“说得通，”她说，“它有前科。”
# en: The prefect writes down every word you say, then doubles the fine for "contempt of librarian". You pay it, and a demerit besides.
opt.right.say.2 [a6947d] = 级长把你说的每个字都记了下来，然后以“藐视图书管理员”为由把罚款翻倍。你交了钱，还顺带吃了一个记过。

@event inc_letter_home
# en: Bad Weather at Home
title [ae05d8] = 家里遭了风雨
# en: A letter from home, written in a hurry. A storm took half the roof, and the repairs will cost more than anyone has. Nobody asks you for anything. That's how you know it's bad.
text [0fccb4] = 一封家信，字迹潦草。一场暴风雨掀掉了半边屋顶，修缮的花费比谁手头的钱都多。没有人向你开口要任何东西。正因如此，你知道情况很糟。
# en: A student at a window reading a rain-spotted letter, a small pile of coins on the sill beside them.
scene [e9924d] = 一个学生站在窗边读一封落了雨点的信，窗台上放着一小堆硬币。
# en: Send crowns home
opt.left.label [ca82d0] = 往家里寄克朗
# en: You send everything you can spare and a little you can't. The reply comes a month later: a drawing of a roof, finished, and a pressed flower.
opt.left.say.1 [bf78ca] = 你寄出了所有能省下的钱，还多寄了一点省不下的。一个月后回信来了：一张画着修好的屋顶的画，还有一朵压干的花。
# en: Write back with love, not money
opt.right.label [f26600] = 回信寄去爱，不寄钱
# en: You write four pages and keep your purse. The reply is kind. It doesn't mention the roof. That night you lie awake and listen to the rain.
opt.right.say.1 [75b549] = 你写了四页信，钱袋没动。回信很温柔，只字未提屋顶。那晚你躺着睡不着，听了一夜的雨。

@event inc_stolen_purse
# en: Market Day Fingers
title [597745] = 集市日的快手
# en: Somewhere between the cheese stall and the man selling enchanted socks, your purse stops being yours. You catch a grey hood slipping between the stalls, already three stalls ahead.
text [2d2565] = 在奶酪摊和那个卖魔法袜子的男人之间的某处，你的钱袋不再属于你了。你瞥见一顶灰色兜帽在摊位间溜走，已经领先你三个摊位。
# en: A crowded village square on market day, a figure in a grey hood slipping away between the stalls with a small purse.
scene [50e0d7] = 集市日拥挤的小镇广场上，一个戴灰兜帽的身影拿着一只小钱袋从摊位间溜走。
# en: Run after the hood
opt.left.label [3e6b9b] = 追那顶兜帽
# en: You corner the thief behind the bakery. The purse comes back a little lighter; they'd already spent some on a bun. You let them keep the bun.
opt.left.say.1 [8a1779] = 你在面包房后面堵住了小偷。钱袋还回来时轻了一点——他们已经拿去买了个面包。你让他们留着那个面包。
# en: You trip over a goose, then a second goose. When you get up, the hood is gone, and so are your crowns.
opt.left.say.2 [52dac0] = 你被一只鹅绊倒，接着又是第二只鹅。等你爬起来，兜帽不见了，你的克朗也不见了。
# en: Let it go
opt.right.label [7a5d2f] = 算了吧
# en: You tell yourself it's only money. You tell yourself that all the way back up the hill, and it never quite takes.
opt.right.say.1 [78bd08] = 你告诉自己，不过是钱而已。你一路走回山上都这么告诉自己，可始终没能真的说服自己。

@event inc_hiccuping_robe
# en: The Robe That Hiccups
title [2955d6] = 会打嗝的长袍
# en: A cauldron two benches down boils over, and a whole batch of Draught of Unending Hiccups soaks your best robe. The stain fades by supper. The hiccups don't. Every few minutes, the robe jumps.
text [291843] = 隔着两张实验台的一口坩埚沸溢了，一整锅“无尽打嗝药剂”泼透了你最好的长袍。污渍到晚饭时就褪了，打嗝却没停。每隔几分钟，长袍就要跳一下。
# en: A student in potion-stained robes jolting mid-step as their robe gives a visible hiccup, classmates hiding smiles.
scene [26b228] = 一个穿着沾满药渍长袍的学生走到一半猛地一颤，长袍明显打了个嗝，同学们憋着笑。
# en: Buy a new robe
opt.left.label [ce85a0] = 买件新长袍
# en: The tailor in the village fits you in an afternoon and charges you for a week. The old robe now hiccups quietly in the bottom of your trunk.
opt.left.say.1 [0564c8] = 山下小镇的裁缝一个下午就给你量好做好，却收了一周的工钱。旧长袍如今在你箱底悄悄地打着嗝。
# en: Wear it with dignity
opt.right.label [1a8893] = 体面地穿着它
# en: {~It hiccups through a lecture on silence.|It hiccups through the headmistress's announcements.} Someone starts a tally on the common-room wall. You are briefly famous for the wrong reasons.
opt.right.say.1 [20fdad] = {~它在一堂讲沉默的课上一路打嗝。|它在院长讲话时一路打嗝。}有人在公共休息室的墙上开始记次数。你短暂地出了名，原因却不太对。

@event patron_tournament_purse
# en: A Patron's Purse
title [21cf49] = 赞助人的奖金袋
# en: The Spring Tournament committee has a velvet cushion, a very thin prize purse and a list of patrons with a lot of room left on it. Patrons are read out before the first bout, in a loud voice, to the whole academy.
text [eebe25] = 春季锦标赛筹委会有一块天鹅绒垫子、一只瘪瘪的奖金袋，还有一份空着大片位置的赞助人名单。第一场比赛前，赞助人的名字会被高声念给全学院听。
# en: A festival committee table on a lawn, a thin purse on a velvet cushion and a list of patrons with plenty of space left.
scene [614979] = 草坪上一张节庆筹委会的桌子，天鹅绒垫子上放着一只瘪瘪的钱袋，旁边一份还空着很多位置的赞助人名单。
# en: Fund the champion's purse
opt.left.label [151eb5] = 包下冠军奖金
# en: {~Your name is read out first, and mispronounced only slightly.|Your name rings across the lawn before the first bout. Two first-years bow to you, unsure why.} The champion thanks you from the podium.
opt.left.say.1 [ce25e1] = {~你的名字第一个被念出来，只念错了一点点。|第一场比赛前，你的名字响彻草坪。两个一年级生朝你鞠躬，也不知为什么。}冠军在领奖台上向你致谢。
# en: Put in a few crowns
opt.right.label [eb6938] = 投几枚克朗
# en: Your name is read out somewhere near the end, between a professor's cat and "a well-wisher". It still counts.
opt.right.say.1 [5b4500] = 你的名字在快结束时被念到，夹在一位教授的猫和“一位好心人”之间。但也算数。

@event patron_ledger_print
# en: Paper for the Press
title [f32e02] = 印刷机要纸
# en: Nessa Quill corners you by the library stairs, holding an empty paper tray like evidence. "Special edition. Biggest story of the term. No paper. You," she says, pointing, "look solvent. Patrons get their name on the masthead."
text [2bc86d] = 内莎·奎尔在图书馆楼梯边把你堵住，举着一只空纸盘，像举着证物。“特刊。本学期最大新闻。没纸了。你，”她指着你说，“看起来有钱。赞助人能上报头。”
# en: A cramped office under a staircase, a groaning printing press, and a young editor holding out an empty paper tray.
scene [a206ca] = 楼梯下一间狭小的办公室，一台呻吟着的印刷机，一位年轻的编辑举着一只空纸盘。
# en: Pay for the whole print run
opt.left.label [451de8] = 包下整期印刷
# en: "Headline: generous student saves free press," Nessa says, already writing it. The masthead lists you in tiny capitals, which she says is the most honour anyone gets.
opt.left.say.1 [079497] = “头条：慷慨学生拯救自由报业，”内莎说着，已经开始写了。报头上用极小的字印着你的名字，她说这已是任何人能得到的最高荣誉。
# en: Buy one small advertisement
opt.right.label [ebad59] = 买一小块广告
# en: You buy a corner of page four. Nessa writes your copy for you, and somehow it reads like a confession. People quote it at you for a week.
opt.right.say.1 [933b10] = 你买下第四版的一个角落。内莎替你写了广告词，不知怎么读起来像一份供词。整整一周都有人对着你念它。

@event donate_greenhouse_glass
# en: The Broken Panes
title [cd7452] = 碎掉的玻璃
# en: Last night's hail went through the greenhouse glass like a hammer through toffee. A collection tin hangs on the gate with a hand-lettered sign: every pane paid for keeps the mandrakes from catching cold.
text [fa105f] = 昨夜的冰雹砸穿温室的玻璃，就像锤子砸进太妃糖。大门上挂着一只募捐罐和一块手写的牌子：每捐一块玻璃，曼德拉草就少一分着凉的危险。
# en: A collection tin on a garden gate, broken glass glittering in the grass behind it and steam escaping from a damaged greenhouse.
scene [45c440] = 花园大门上挂着一只募捐罐，后面草地上碎玻璃闪闪发光，一座破损的温室正往外冒着热气。
# en: Pay for a whole pane
opt.left.label [14b4c4] = 捐一整块玻璃
# en: A gardener with mud to the elbows insists on showing you your pane. Inside it is warm, green and loud with opinions. You are welcome, she says, any morning.
opt.left.say.1 [96b7a3] = 一位泥巴糊到手肘的园丁非要带你去看“你的”那块玻璃。里面温暖、葱绿，满是各种意见。她说，你哪天早上来都欢迎。
# en: Drop in a coin and walk on
opt.right.label [6d6a0e] = 投枚硬币就走
# en: The coin clinks into the tin. Behind the gate, something small and leafy sneezes. You feel, obscurely, that you've been judged.
opt.right.say.1 [e09171] = 硬币叮当落进罐里。大门后，有个小小的、长着叶子的东西打了个喷嚏。你隐约觉得自己被评判了。

@event donate_duel_floor
# en: The Scorched Floor
title [47b123] = 烧焦的地板
# en: A duellist with a bandaged hand rattles a box at the foot of the east stair. "The hall floor," he says. "Someone set it on fire again. Every board you buy, we carve your initials on the underside. Honour, and splinters."
text [d8070e] = 一个手上缠着绷带的决斗者在东楼梯脚下摇着一只箱子。“大厅的地板，”他说，“又有人把它点着了。你买一块板，我们就把你的姓名缩写刻在背面。荣誉，外加木刺。”
# en: A sweaty duellist with a collection box at the foot of a stair, scorched floorboards stacked behind them.
scene [ea8375] = 一个满头大汗的决斗者在楼梯脚下捧着募捐箱，身后堆着烧焦的地板。
# en: Buy a row of floorboards
opt.left.label [a3aa26] = 买下一整排地板
# en: He drags you upstairs to see. The hall smells of smoke and wax, and the practice dummies glare at you. Your initials go on the underside of the board by the door.
opt.left.say.1 [58bb9f] = 他拽着你上楼去看。大厅里一股烟和蜡的味道，练习假人们瞪着你。你的姓名缩写刻在了门边那块板的背面。
# en: Give him a coin for the bandage
opt.right.label [849d48] = 给他一枚硬币买绷带
# en: He thanks you with exaggerated courtesy and goes back to rattling. Somewhere above, steel rings on steel, and nobody invites you up.
opt.right.say.1 [c52343] = 他夸张地向你行礼致谢，又回去接着摇箱子。楼上某处传来钢铁相击的声音，没有人邀请你上去。

@event xchg_arrival
# en: Guests in Green
title [d9ca04] = 身着绿袍的客人
# en: Four students in Thornwick green arrive for a term, with trunks and very polite smiles. Within an hour every portrait in the entrance hall is winking at the wrong people. A prefect looks around for someone, anyone, to show them the castle.
text [5855c8] = 四个穿着荆木绿袍的学生来这里待一个学期，带着箱子和非常客气的笑容。不到一个小时，门厅里每一幅肖像都在冲错的人眨眼。一位级长四处张望，想找个人——随便谁——带他们参观城堡。
# en: Four students in green Thornwick robes standing in a grand entrance hall, the portraits on the walls all turned to stare at them.
scene [4447a8] = 四个穿绿色荆木长袍的学生站在宏伟的门厅里，墙上的肖像全都转过头盯着他们。
# en: Offer to show them round
opt.left.label [52352b] = 主动带他们参观
# en: You give the full tour, moving stairs included. By the end the boy with the sketchbook admits Lumenhold's towers are "not as crooked as reported".
opt.left.say.1 [110d38] = 你带他们走完了全程，移动楼梯也算在内。最后那个拿速写本的男生承认，流明堡的塔“没有传闻中那么歪”。
# en: Halfway round, they convince you a wall is a door. It isn't. They are very sorry, and laughing too hard to say so.
opt.left.say.2 [5cd71f] = 走到一半，他们让你相信一面墙是一扇门。它不是。他们非常抱歉，只是笑得太厉害，说不出口。
# en: Watch them from a distance
opt.right.label [e05dd0] = 远远地观察他们
# en: You watch them all week. They watch back. You learn that the quiet one counts doorways, and that they know you're watching.
opt.right.say.1 [175ece] = 你观察了他们整整一周。他们也观察你。你发现那个安静的人会数门洞，也发现他们知道你在看。

@event xchg_ink_cuffs
# en: The Ink-Stained Cuffs
title [a6af14] = 沾墨的袖口
# en: Late in the library, you find the Thornwick girl with the ink-stained cuffs copying from a chained book she shouldn't have reached. She sees you see her. "It's only history," she says. "Unless you want it to be a scandal."
text [2833d3] = 深夜的图书馆里，你撞见那个袖口沾着墨迹的荆木女生正在抄一本她本不该够得着的锁链书。她看见你看见了她。“只是历史而已，”她说，“除非你想让它变成丑闻。”
# en: A library at dusk, a student in green robes with ink-stained cuffs copying from a book chained to a desk.
scene [00e6b0] = 黄昏的图书馆，一个袖口沾墨的绿袍学生正从一本锁在桌上的书里抄写。
# en: Report her to the librarian
opt.left.label [c73db6] = 向管理员举报她
# en: The librarian thanks you, coldly. The Thornwick girl is confined to the guest wing for a week. She nods to you at dinner afterwards, as if you had both played well.
opt.left.say.1 [66098b] = 图书管理员冷冷地向你道了谢。那个荆木女生被禁足在客房区一周。之后的晚饭上她朝你点点头，好像你们俩都下了一手好棋。
# en: Keep quiet, for a favour
opt.right.label [cca079] = 保持沉默，换个人情
# en: She tears out the page she copied and hands you the other half of her notes instead. "We're even," she says. You're fairly sure you aren't.
opt.right.say.1 [ee5c42] = 她撕下抄好的那页，转而把自己笔记的另一半递给你。“我们扯平了，”她说。你很确定并没有。

@event xchg_farewell
# en: A Thornwick Farewell
title [7e24b5] = 荆木的告别
# en: The Thornwick students leave on the dawn barge. The boy with the sketchbook finds you on the jetty and holds out his scarf. "It's a custom," he says. "Probably. I've just decided." Behind him his friends pretend not to listen.
text [2522b5] = 荆木的学生们要乘黎明的驳船离开。拿速写本的男生在栈桥上找到你，递出他的围巾。“这是个习俗，”他说，“大概吧。我刚决定的。”他身后的朋友们假装没在听。
# en: Students in green and blue robes on a jetty at dawn, a barge waiting, one of them holding out a striped scarf.
scene [75f77e] = 黎明时分的栈桥上，穿绿袍和蓝袍的学生们站着，一艘驳船在等，其中一人递出一条条纹围巾。
# en: Swap scarves
opt.left.label [1fdbff] = 交换围巾
# en: You trade scarves on the jetty. Someone from your own house mutters "traitor" at breakfast. You wear it anyway, and get a letter from across the hills by the end of the month.
opt.left.say.1 [5d5b9e] = 你们在栈桥上交换了围巾。早饭时，你自己学院的某人嘀咕了一句“叛徒”。你照样围着它，月底前还收到了一封翻山而来的信。
# en: Challenge him to one last duel
opt.right.label [07d107] = 邀他最后决斗一场
# en: You win, narrowly, on the wet boards. He laughs, bows, and sketches you mid-spell on the barge as it pulls away. The sketch arrives by post, flattering.
opt.right.say.1 [debf60] = 你在湿漉漉的木板上险胜。他大笑着鞠了一躬，驳船离岸时还在给施法中的你画速写。那张速写后来寄到了，画得相当美化。
# en: He wins with an illusion of a second you. You both end up in the lake. It is, somehow, the best goodbye you've had.
opt.right.say.2 [cbf2ca] = 他用一个“第二个你”的幻象赢了。你们俩最后都掉进了湖里。不知怎么，这竟是你经历过最好的一次告别。
